 "title": "Saccharomyces cerevisiae Metabolism and Regulation Network",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around Saccharomyces cerevisiae, a yeast organism, and its interactions with various chemicals and other organisms. The yeast is involved in the metabolism of sulfur-containing compounds, including cysteine, methionine, and homocysteine, which are catabolized and assimilated through various pathways. The yeast also interacts with other organisms, such as Candida albicans, and is exposed to chemicals like ZnS QDs and ZnSO4. The cluster highlights the importance of Met32, a gene or protein, in regulating various processes, including the activation of Jlp12 and the regulation of Sod1. The network also shows the role of HSU1 in sulfide metabolism and the pleiotropic effects of sulfate on the yeast.",
